IMPORT prelude

-- Financial Advisers Act 2001 (Singapore) -- the conduct rules a client can rely on: false or misleading statements (s 35), the
-- reasonable basis for a recommendation (s 36), the effect of a contravention on the transaction (s 39), insurance broking
-- accounts (s 41), placing risk with unlicensed insurers (s 42), misrepresentations on proposal and claim forms (s 43), and
-- disclosure of interests in circulars (s 45).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/FAA2001.txt. The 2020 Revised Edition
-- renumbered the Act: the reasonable-basis rule, long known as s 27, is s 36 here (the deposit carries the old numbers in
-- brackets).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 15 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to conduct towards clients. Not
-- encoded: licensing and exemption (Part 2), representatives, the MAS powers, the notices and guidelines under s 74 (where most
-- conduct detail lives), and the regulations (not retrieved).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Financial Advisers Act 2001 -- conduct`

§§ `35 -- false or misleading statements`

-- s 35(1): a licensed financial adviser must not make a false or misleading statement about amounts payable, the effect of a
-- contract, or "in connection with the provision of any financial advisory service", if it does not care whether it is true or
-- "knows or OUGHT REASONABLY TO HAVE KNOWN" it is false. (5): omitting a material matter counts.
-- (3): a person who reasonably relied on it and suffered loss may recover damages. (6): an offence "even if a contract does not
-- come into being" -- $50,000 or 12 months.
DECLARE Statement HAS
    `false or misleading, or omitted a material matter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the adviser knew, ought to have known, or did not care` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the client relied on it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the reliance was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the client suffered loss` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the statement` IS A Statement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the statement contravenes section 35` IF
    `the statement`'s `false or misleading, or omitted a material matter` AND `the statement`'s `the adviser knew, ought to have known, or did not care`

GIVEN `the statement` IS A Statement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the client can claim damages for the statement` IF
        `the statement contravenes section 35` `the statement`
    AND `the statement`'s `the client relied on it`
    AND `the statement`'s `the reliance was reasonable`
    AND `the statement`'s `the client suffered loss`

§§ `36 -- reasonable basis`

-- s 36(1): an adviser must not recommend an investment product to a person who may reasonably be expected to rely on it without a
-- "reasonable basis". (2): there is none unless the adviser, "having regard to the information possessed by the [adviser]
-- concerning the investment objectives, financial situation and particular needs of the person", gave such consideration to and
-- investigation of the product as is reasonable, AND based the recommendation on it. (3): damages for reasonable reliance and loss.
-- (4): a recommendation may be express or implied. (5): prescribed exemptions.
DECLARE Recommendation HAS
    `considered the client's objectives, situation and needs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `investigated the product reasonably` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the recommendation was based on that work` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the client relied reasonably` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the client suffered loss` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the recommendation` IS A Recommendation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a reasonable basis` IF
        `the recommendation`'s `considered the client's objectives, situation and needs`
    AND `the recommendation`'s `investigated the product reasonably`
    AND `the recommendation`'s `the recommendation was based on that work`

GIVEN `the recommendation` IS A Recommendation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the client can claim damages for the recommendation` IF
        (NOT `there is a reasonable basis` `the recommendation`)
    AND `the recommendation`'s `the client relied reasonably`
    AND `the recommendation`'s `the client suffered loss`

§§ `39 -- the transaction stands`

-- s 39(1): "a contravention of any requirement of this Act ... does NOT AFFECT THE VALIDITY OR ENFORCEABILITY of any agreement,
-- transaction or arrangement" (subject to express provision otherwise). (2): nor does breach of a code or guideline.
--
-- A client sold an unsuitable product keeps the product. The remedy under ss 35(3) and 36(3) is damages, not rescission under
-- this Act.
GIVEN `the adviser contravened the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract remains enforceable` IF TRUE

§§ `41 to 43 -- insurance`

-- s 41(3): a lien or claim on an insurance broking premium account is void "unless the moneys ... are for fees due and owing to
-- the licensed financial adviser"; (4) any charge or mortgage over it is void.
-- s 42(1): an adviser must not negotiate insurance except with a licensed insurer; (2) except reinsurance and risks outside
-- Singapore; (4) or with MAS permission. $25,000 or 3 years.
-- s 43: with intent to deceive, writing a false matter on a proposal or claim form, or advising or inducing the client to do so
-- or to omit a material matter -- $25,000 or 12 months, "even if a contract of insurance does not come into being".
DECLARE Security IS ONE OF
    `a lien for the adviser's unpaid fees`
    `a lien for a debt owed by the client on another matter`
    `a charge in favour of the adviser's bank`

GIVEN `the security` IS A Security
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the security over the premium account is valid` IF
    CONSIDER `the security`
    WHEN `a lien for the adviser's unpaid fees` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE Placement IS ONE OF
    `a licensed insurer`
    `an unlicensed insurer for a Singapore risk`
    `an unlicensed insurer for reinsurance`
    `an unlicensed insurer for an overseas risk`

GIVEN `the placement` IS A Placement, `MAS permitted it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the placement is lawful` IF
        `MAS permitted it`
    OR  CONSIDER `the placement`
        WHEN `an unlicensed insurer for a Singapore risk` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `told the client to leave out a pre-existing condition` IS A BOOLEAN, `with intent to deceive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the adviser commits a section 43 offence` IF
    `told the client to leave out a pre-existing condition` AND `with intent to deceive`

§§ `45 -- disclosure of interests`

-- s 45(1): a circular recommending specified products must state concisely any interest the adviser or a connected person has in
-- them. (2): defence -- not aware and could not reasonably be expected to be aware. (3)(b): an underwriter is deemed interested.
-- (4): keep a copy for 5 years.
GIVEN `had an interest` IS A BOOLEAN, `disclosed it` IS A BOOLEAN, `could not reasonably have known` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the circular contravenes section 45` IF
    `had an interest` AND (NOT `disclosed it`) AND (NOT `could not reasonably have known`)
